1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,164
Here is a mistake that has ended careers.

2
00:00:03,164 --> 00:00:06,153
Someone commits a file with a password inside,

3
00:00:06,153 --> 00:00:06,803
pushes it,

4
00:00:06,803 --> 00:00:09,077
and the password is now in history,

5
00:00:09,077 --> 00:00:09,922
for everyone,

6
00:00:09,922 --> 00:00:10,441
forever.

7
00:00:10,991 --> 00:00:13,441
Last lesson you made your first commits.

8
00:00:13,441 --> 00:00:16,136
Today you get control of them: what goes in,

9
00:00:16,136 --> 00:00:17,055
what stays out,

10
00:00:17,055 --> 00:00:18,586
and how to read the past.

11
00:00:19,136 --> 00:00:20,043
Three skills.

12
00:00:20,043 --> 00:00:20,602
Staging,

13
00:00:20,602 --> 00:00:23,255
so each commit holds one clean change.

14
00:00:23,255 --> 00:00:23,813
History,

15
00:00:23,813 --> 00:00:26,675
so you can find who changed what and why.

16
00:00:26,675 --> 00:00:27,862
And ignore files,

17
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:30,165
so junk and secrets never get in.

18
00:00:30,715 --> 00:00:33,531
As always, there is a lab with a checker at the end.

19
00:00:35,581 --> 00:00:35,950
First,

20
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:36,320
a map.

21
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:39,276
Git compares three snapshots: your working tree,

22
00:00:39,276 --> 00:00:40,323
the staging area,

23
00:00:40,323 --> 00:00:41,554
and the last commit.

24
00:00:42,104 --> 00:00:46,554
Git diff with no options compares the working tree to the staging area.

25
00:00:46,554 --> 00:00:49,123
It shows changes you have not staged yet.

26
00:00:49,673 --> 00:00:53,919
Git diff dash dash staged compares the staging area to the last commit.

27
00:00:53,919 --> 00:00:56,969
It shows exactly what the next commit will contain.

28
00:00:57,519 --> 00:01:01,807
And git diff head compares your working tree to the last commit, staged or not.

29
00:01:02,357 --> 00:01:03,600
Before every commit,

30
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,464
run git diff dash dash staged.

31
00:01:05,464 --> 00:01:08,074
It is your last chance to catch a mistake.

32
00:01:10,124 --> 00:01:15,052
Let us see it live. This project has one commit. Go in. Type: CD, site.

33
00:01:15,602 --> 00:01:19,357
Ask for the short status. Type: git status, dash S.

34
00:01:19,907 --> 00:01:20,615
Two files.

35
00:01:20,615 --> 00:01:23,235
The first column is the staging area,

36
00:01:23,235 --> 00:01:25,430
the second is the working tree.

37
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:27,555
A space then M means modified,

38
00:01:27,555 --> 00:01:28,334
not staged.

39
00:01:28,334 --> 00:01:30,742
Two question marks mean untracked.

40
00:01:30,742 --> 00:01:32,583
Look at the change itself.

41
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:33,645
Type: git diff.

42
00:01:34,195 --> 00:01:36,089
Minus lines were removed,

43
00:01:36,089 --> 00:01:37,755
plus lines were added.

44
00:01:37,755 --> 00:01:39,345
Stage just this file.

45
00:01:39,345 --> 00:01:40,405
Type: git add,

46
00:01:40,405 --> 00:01:41,769
index dot H T M L.

47
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:45,519
Staged. Now the plain diff again. Type: git diff.

48
00:01:46,069 --> 00:01:46,481
Empty.

49
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:48,752
Everything changed is now staged,

50
00:01:48,752 --> 00:01:50,815
so nothing is left to compare.

51
00:01:50,815 --> 00:01:53,361
Now ask what the commit will contain.

52
00:01:53,361 --> 00:01:54,393
Type: git diff,

53
00:01:54,393 --> 00:01:55,562
dash dash staged.

54
00:01:56,112 --> 00:01:57,255
The same change,

55
00:01:57,255 --> 00:01:59,541
now waiting in the staging area.

56
00:01:59,541 --> 00:02:00,755
Check the status.

57
00:02:00,755 --> 00:02:01,969
Type: git status,

58
00:02:01,969 --> 00:02:02,469
dash S.

59
00:02:03,019 --> 00:02:05,069
M in the first column: staged.

60
00:02:05,069 --> 00:02:07,393
The stylesheet is still untracked,

61
00:02:07,393 --> 00:02:09,511
so it stays out of this commit.

62
00:02:09,511 --> 00:02:12,996
That is how you keep one logical change per commit.

63
00:02:12,996 --> 00:02:15,320
If you stage something by mistake,

64
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,208
take it back.

65
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:17,438
Type: git restore,

66
00:02:17,438 --> 00:02:18,600
dash dash staged,

67
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,830
index dot H T M L.

68
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:20,955
Restore,

69
00:02:20,955 --> 00:02:22,538
with dash dash staged,

70
00:02:22,538 --> 00:02:25,702
only moves the file out of the staging area.

71
00:02:25,702 --> 00:02:26,997
Your edit is safe.

72
00:02:26,997 --> 00:02:28,147
Check once more.

73
00:02:28,147 --> 00:02:29,370
Type: git status,

74
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:29,873
dash S.

75
00:02:30,423 --> 00:02:32,760
Back to a space and an M: modified,

76
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:33,495
not staged.

77
00:02:33,495 --> 00:02:34,630
Nothing was lost.

78
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:38,637
Staging is a safe workspace for building the perfect commit.

79
00:02:40,687 --> 00:02:42,026
Now the commit message.

80
00:02:42,026 --> 00:02:43,016
Your future self,

81
00:02:43,016 --> 00:02:43,831
and your team,

82
00:02:43,831 --> 00:02:46,276
will read it more than they read the code.

83
00:02:46,826 --> 00:02:48,559
One: a short subject line,

84
00:02:48,559 --> 00:02:50,092
about fifty characters,

85
00:02:50,092 --> 00:02:52,358
in the imperative: Add stylesheet,

86
00:02:52,358 --> 00:02:54,357
not Added stylesheet or stuff.

87
00:02:54,907 --> 00:02:56,108
Two: a blank line,

88
00:02:56,108 --> 00:02:56,441
then,

89
00:02:56,441 --> 00:02:57,108
if needed,

90
00:02:57,108 --> 00:02:58,775
a body that explains why,

91
00:02:58,775 --> 00:02:59,376
not what.

92
00:02:59,376 --> 00:03:01,243
The diff already shows what.

93
00:03:01,793 --> 00:03:04,078
Three: one logical change per commit.

94
00:03:04,078 --> 00:03:06,611
If you need the word and in your subject,

95
00:03:06,611 --> 00:03:08,278
it is probably two commits.

96
00:03:08,828 --> 00:03:14,226
A good history is a readable story. A bad one is a pile of messages that say fix.

97
00:03:16,276 --> 00:03:21,353
Now read the past. This project has four commits. Go in. Type: CD, site.

98
00:03:21,903 --> 00:03:25,999
Start with the compact view. Type: git log, dash dash one line.

99
00:03:26,549 --> 00:03:27,428
Newest first,

100
00:03:27,428 --> 00:03:28,373
one line each.

101
00:03:28,373 --> 00:03:31,346
For the full detail of the last two commits.

102
00:03:31,346 --> 00:03:32,292
Type: git log,

103
00:03:32,292 --> 00:03:32,764
dash N,

104
00:03:32,764 --> 00:03:33,035
two.

105
00:03:33,585 --> 00:03:35,674
Each commit shows its full hash,

106
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:36,392
the author,

107
00:03:36,392 --> 00:03:38,024
the date and the message.

108
00:03:38,024 --> 00:03:39,656
You can see who and when.

109
00:03:39,656 --> 00:03:42,137
To see what changed in the top commit.

110
00:03:42,137 --> 00:03:43,116
Type: git show,

111
00:03:43,116 --> 00:03:44,096
dash dash stat,

112
00:03:44,096 --> 00:03:44,422
head.

113
00:03:44,972 --> 00:03:45,758
The header,

114
00:03:45,758 --> 00:03:47,545
then which files changed,

115
00:03:47,545 --> 00:03:48,903
and how many lines.

116
00:03:48,903 --> 00:03:51,833
Now follow a single file through history.

117
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:52,834
Type: git log,

118
00:03:52,834 --> 00:03:54,192
dash dash one line,

119
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:54,907
dash dash,

120
00:03:54,907 --> 00:03:56,193
index dot H T M L.

121
00:03:56,743 --> 00:03:59,402
Only the commits that touched that file.

122
00:03:59,402 --> 00:04:02,328
The two dashes mean: what follows is a path.

123
00:04:02,328 --> 00:04:05,784
Now see the file as it was in the very first commit.

124
00:04:05,784 --> 00:04:09,042
Head tilde three means three commits before head.

125
00:04:09,042 --> 00:04:10,039
Type: git show,

126
00:04:10,039 --> 00:04:11,169
head tilde three,

127
00:04:11,169 --> 00:04:11,568
colon,

128
00:04:11,568 --> 00:04:12,765
index dot H T M L.

129
00:04:13,315 --> 00:04:14,567
The original file,

130
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:16,863
even though it has changed since.

131
00:04:16,863 --> 00:04:19,854
Last tool for the detective: for each line,

132
00:04:19,854 --> 00:04:21,872
which commit last changed it.

133
00:04:21,872 --> 00:04:22,985
Type: git blame,

134
00:04:22,985 --> 00:04:24,237
index dot H T M L.

135
00:04:24,787 --> 00:04:25,367
Each line,

136
00:04:25,367 --> 00:04:26,294
with the commit,

137
00:04:26,294 --> 00:04:27,685
the author and the date.

138
00:04:27,685 --> 00:04:29,250
When something looks wrong,

139
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:31,453
blame tells you where to start asking.

140
00:04:31,453 --> 00:04:32,960
It is about understanding,

141
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,409
not about blaming people.

142
00:04:36,459 --> 00:04:37,941
Now keeping junk out.

143
00:04:37,941 --> 00:04:43,517
This project has a debug log and a build folder that should never be committed.

144
00:04:43,517 --> 00:04:43,940
Go in.

145
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:44,575
Type: CD,

146
00:04:44,575 --> 00:04:44,928
site.

147
00:04:45,478 --> 00:04:48,785
Ask what Git sees. Type: git status, dash S.

148
00:04:49,335 --> 00:04:52,540
The build folder and the log show as untracked,

149
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:57,721
and the modified file is a cache file that was committed by mistake earlier.

150
00:04:57,721 --> 00:04:59,221
First the ignore file.

151
00:04:59,221 --> 00:04:59,971
Type: echo,

152
00:04:59,971 --> 00:05:00,926
debug dot log,

153
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:02,903
redirect into dot git ignore.

154
00:05:03,453 --> 00:05:05,152
Now add the build folder,

155
00:05:05,152 --> 00:05:06,035
with a slash,

156
00:05:06,035 --> 00:05:07,598
so it matches a folder.

157
00:05:07,598 --> 00:05:09,297
Use two arrows to append.

158
00:05:09,297 --> 00:05:10,044
Type: echo,

159
00:05:10,044 --> 00:05:10,860
build slash,

160
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:11,607
two arrows,

161
00:05:11,607 --> 00:05:12,626
dot git ignore.

162
00:05:13,176 --> 00:05:15,438
Check. Type: git status, dash S.

163
00:05:15,988 --> 00:05:17,207
Both disappeared.

164
00:05:17,207 --> 00:05:19,718
Only the ignore file itself is new,

165
00:05:19,718 --> 00:05:23,663
and you commit that so the whole team shares the rules.

166
00:05:23,663 --> 00:05:25,529
Ask why a file is ignored.

167
00:05:25,529 --> 00:05:27,537
Type: git check dash ignore,

168
00:05:27,537 --> 00:05:28,039
dash V,

169
00:05:28,039 --> 00:05:29,044
debug dot log.

170
00:05:29,594 --> 00:05:30,838
It names the file,

171
00:05:30,838 --> 00:05:31,945
the line number,

172
00:05:31,945 --> 00:05:33,466
and the exact pattern.

173
00:05:33,466 --> 00:05:34,987
Perfect for debugging.

174
00:05:34,987 --> 00:05:35,886
Now the trap.

175
00:05:35,886 --> 00:05:38,237
The cache file is already tracked.

176
00:05:38,237 --> 00:05:40,035
Add it to the ignore file.

177
00:05:40,035 --> 00:05:40,796
Type: echo,

178
00:05:40,796 --> 00:05:41,833
cache dot temp,

179
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:42,594
two arrows,

180
00:05:42,594 --> 00:05:43,631
dot git ignore.

181
00:05:44,181 --> 00:05:47,338
Check the status. Type: git status, dash S.

182
00:05:47,888 --> 00:05:48,999
Still modified!

183
00:05:48,999 --> 00:05:52,185
Ignore rules only apply to untracked files.

184
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:55,149
A file Git already tracks stays tracked.

185
00:05:55,149 --> 00:05:56,631
To stop tracking it,

186
00:05:56,631 --> 00:05:58,112
but keep it on disk.

187
00:05:58,112 --> 00:05:59,150
Type: git R M,

188
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,409
dash dash cached,

189
00:06:00,409 --> 00:06:01,520
cache dot temp.

190
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:05,953
Removed from tracking. Check. Type: git status, dash S.

191
00:06:06,503 --> 00:06:10,950
D in the first column: the next commit deletes it from the repository,

192
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:12,983
but the file stays on your disk.

193
00:06:12,983 --> 00:06:16,287
One more warning: if a secret was already committed,

194
00:06:16,287 --> 00:06:17,939
ignoring it is not enough.

195
00:06:17,939 --> 00:06:19,210
It stays in history,

196
00:06:19,210 --> 00:06:21,116
so you must rotate the secret.

197
00:06:21,116 --> 00:06:23,911
We cover cleaning history in a later lesson.

198
00:06:26,061 --> 00:06:28,834
Your task, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

199
00:06:29,384 --> 00:06:31,944
The lab is lab fifty-eight dot S H,

200
00:06:31,944 --> 00:06:35,675
in the academy slash lab folder of git hub dot com,

201
00:06:35,675 --> 00:06:37,137
slash it dash waves,

202
00:06:37,137 --> 00:06:38,820
slash dev ops dash A I.

203
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,502
Install it like before,

204
00:06:40,502 --> 00:06:41,672
then run lab up.

205
00:06:42,222 --> 00:06:46,015
It builds a repository with a real change to app dot conf,

206
00:06:46,015 --> 00:06:47,454
a personal notes file,

207
00:06:47,454 --> 00:06:48,173
junk files,

208
00:06:48,173 --> 00:06:51,246
and a cache file that was committed by mistake.

209
00:06:51,796 --> 00:06:54,669
One: create a dot git ignore so the debug log,

210
00:06:54,669 --> 00:06:57,791
the secrets file and the build folder are ignored.

211
00:06:58,341 --> 00:07:02,096
Two: stop tracking cache dot temp, but keep the file on disk.

212
00:07:02,646 --> 00:07:05,316
Three: commit only the app dot conf change,

213
00:07:05,316 --> 00:07:06,620
with a clear message.

214
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,918
The notes file must stay uncommitted.

215
00:07:09,468 --> 00:07:11,102
Four: in answers dot text,

216
00:07:11,102 --> 00:07:15,441
write one number: how many commits touched app dot conf before yours.

217
00:07:15,991 --> 00:07:17,257
Then run lab check.

218
00:07:17,257 --> 00:07:18,322
Four pass lines.

219
00:07:18,322 --> 00:07:19,521
Before you commit,

220
00:07:19,521 --> 00:07:21,986
always run git diff dash dash staged.

221
00:07:24,036 --> 00:07:26,020
Six points, and you need all six.

222
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:28,405
The checker shows four pass lines.

223
00:07:28,955 --> 00:07:32,880
You reviewed the commit with git diff dash dash staged before committing.

224
00:07:33,430 --> 00:07:36,011
The commit message is clear, in the imperative.

225
00:07:36,561 --> 00:07:39,655
You can explain why ignoring a tracked file does nothing.

226
00:07:40,205 --> 00:07:42,530
The number in answers dot text is correct.

227
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,723
You ran lab down to clean up.

228
00:07:45,273 --> 00:07:46,894
To pass, you need all six.

229
00:07:48,944 --> 00:07:51,781
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

230
00:07:52,331 --> 00:07:54,550
One: install the lab, and run lab up.

231
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:59,025
Two: write the ignore file, and check it with git check dash ignore.

232
00:07:59,575 --> 00:08:01,325
Three: untrack the cache file.

233
00:08:01,875 --> 00:08:05,267
Four: stage only app dot conf, review it, and commit.

234
00:08:05,817 --> 00:08:09,785
Five: find the answer with git log for that file, and run lab check.

235
00:08:10,335 --> 00:08:11,807
Six: run lab down.

236
00:08:12,357 --> 00:08:14,191
Pause the video, and begin now.

237
00:08:29,741 --> 00:08:30,616
Quick check.

238
00:08:31,166 --> 00:08:33,768
Which command shows what the next commit will contain?

239
00:08:34,318 --> 00:08:36,729
How do you take a file out of the staging area?

240
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:39,818
Why does ignoring a tracked file change nothing?

241
00:08:40,368 --> 00:08:42,565
How do you follow the history of one file?

242
00:08:43,115 --> 00:08:49,280
Objective covered: M C zero seven, objective two, staging, history, and ignore files.

243
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,900
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

244
00:09:02,450 --> 00:09:04,988
Next: branches, merging, and conflicts.

245
00:09:05,538 --> 00:09:08,866
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
